      "writtenOn": "2016-08-11T08:08:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "yeah, I looked at doing that a few times. Since it\u0027s not implemented a single select loop, you\u0027ve got to check for errors in the pipeline much more often, otherwise you run into the danger of filling up the queues and blocking. That\u0027s still somewhat of a problem now, but since it\u0027s not on the main thread, as long as we print out the error, this goroutine can get stuck and we\u0027ll still be fine.",
      "parentUuid": "f927ab96_a9ac79f3",
      "revId": "a169de21c613490b357d848cb61b24a6e9cd60a4",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
